# SCAFFOLD_MANIFEST — the one place that says what goes into a project.
#
# This file exists because the list used to live in four places: the script,
# both routes in MAKERS_INSTRUCTIONS.md, ADOPT_EXISTING.md and README.md. They
# had already drifted at one commit old — one route copied MAKERS_INSTRUCTIONS
# and the other did not, and README's list copied mutate.sh WITHOUT
# _mutate_apply.py, which mutate.sh cannot run without.
#
# That is PLAYBOOK.md section 8: if state is written in more than one place, it
# will drift, and the cure is structural rather than a fifth careful copy.
#
# Format, one per line:
#     SOURCE:DEST            copied verbatim
#     SOURCE:DEST:render     copied with __NAME__, __YEAR__ and __HOLDER__
#                            substituted
#     SOURCE:DEST:new-only   only for a NEW project, skipped by --files-only,
#                            because it would overwrite work in an existing one
#     SOURCE:DEST:keep-existing  copied only when DEST does not already exist
#
# tools/selftest.sh asserts every source exists, that no destination is claimed
# twice, that the documents carry no rival copy of this list, and that nothing
# ships with an unsubstituted placeholder still in it.

PLAYBOOK.md:PLAYBOOK.md
MAKERS_INSTRUCTIONS.md:MAKERS_INSTRUCTIONS.md
.gitattributes:.gitattributes
templates/validate.yml:.github/workflows/validate.yml
templates/CONTRIBUTING.md:CONTRIBUTING.md
tools/mutate.sh:tools/mutate.sh
tools/_mutate_apply.py:tools/_mutate_apply.py
templates/gitignore:.gitignore:keep-existing
templates/README.md:README.md:render:new-only
templates/LICENSE:LICENSE:render:new-only
templates/main.py:main.py:render:new-only
